index 570981a..ddc742a 100644
--- a/rd-agent/README.md
+++ b/rd-agent/README.md
@@ -33,3 +33,63 @@ want to explore the control files.
 more information on the containing projects, visit:
 
   https://github.com/facebookexperimental/resctl-demo
+
+
+## Embedded support-file compatibility (reviewed downstream repair)
+
+This source revision embeds a Python 3 IO-latency collector with the BCC
+C language options required for the anonymous tagged structure members used
+by newer Linux headers. The measurement program itself is unchanged. Generated
+helpers are reconciled with the current executable, including after the
+`--reset` performed by `resctl-bench`; do not maintain fixes only in an emitted
+`misc-bin/` directory, because reset removes those files.
+
+For file-only inspection of the actual executable, as an ordinary user:
+
+```sh
+rd-agent --export-support /existing/parent/new-helper-directory
+```
+
+The destination must not already exist and the option must be used alone.
+This path only exports the five embedded support files. It does not construct
+normal agent configuration, access a disk, run systemd, change swap, attach BPF,
+or run a workload. Normal agent execution still checks the actual BPF collector;
+the export path is not a bypass for benchmark requirements.
+
+`misc::support_tests` includes reset/recreation, stale-file, exact-byte and
+symlink regressions. See the containing build kit's `docs/NATIVE-REPAIR.md` for
+the source patch, compatibility contract and mandatory packaging checks.
+
+### IOCost Lab native repair contract (v3)
+
+`rd-agent --runtime-contract` prints `resctl-iocost-lab-v3` and exits without
+reading configuration or touching systemd, cgroups, BPF, swap or storage. The
+same exact file-only argument is supported by resctl-bench, rd-hashd and
+resctl-demo. Extra arguments are not interpreted as a successful probe.
+
+This repair also distinguishes disabled per-device I/O-controller rows from
+active limits, refreshes sysinfo memory/process snapshots before checks, and
+avoids a secondary collector-disconnect panic during normal shutdown. Real
+active limits and unexpected collector failures still fail closed. Full runs
+require critical D-Bus services already under hostcritical.slice; after
+reviewing placement overrides, reboot a maintenance host instead of restarting
+D-Bus during an active session. resctl-bench returns an ordinary nonzero error
+for a rejected job rather than deliberately panicking on that error.
+
+
+### Exact balloon lifecycle (v3)
+
+The embedded memory-balloon.py is included in support export and side assets.
+Only the native agent controls its lifetime. READY means the requested bytes,
+rounded up to a host page, were fully touched. The transient service uses
+Restart=no and MemorySwapMax=0. It never shrinks/retries its target or reports
+partial readiness. Service identity and policy are checked during hashd
+calibration as well as ordinary execution; unexpected loss/restart is fatal.
+Native resize explicitly stops/resets the previous unit. Stop jobs use replace
+and checked waits so an old queued start cannot conflict with teardown. Ordinary
+command errors propagate after releasing reporter locks, not through panic.
+
+External adaptive/restart drop-ins are incompatible with this measurement
+contract. Restore the old Lab session before starting a fresh v3 run. A compiler
+or file-only export test cannot certify live kernel/systemd behavior; the build
+kit's validation report states which checks have actually been executed.
